  "body": "## Accepted result and published preprint\n\n**A torus-collar proof of the real-spectrum compact-support classification for Nijenhuis operators**, Alec Kriebel. Published paper and verification package: https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23431313 (https://zenodo.org/records/23431313).\n\n<p>This note gives an explicit complete smooth compact-support proof answering the historical Problem 5.11 as printed in arXiv:1804.03737v2. In every dimension n &gt;= 1, precisely the all-real-spectrum Jordan types occur on a nonempty open subset of R^n for globally smooth compactly supported real Nijenhuis operators, with arbitrary prescribed numerical real Jordan data in a commuting local frame. Type and eigenvalues may change elsewhere. The proof gives the full ordered collar equation, finite block removal path, same-dimensional torus embedding and exact zero extension.</p><p>The nonreal obstruction, real semisimple and two-dimensional examples, local arbitrary-type point realizations, and splitting/holomorphic mechanism are credited prior results. A precise zero-point rigidity argument avoids an imprecise polynomial-reduction sentence in the inspected author version; the unread publisher body is not equated to it. Full-result and construction-method priority, novelty and worldwide preexisting openness remain UNKNOWN. This is an attributed complete proof of the printed historical question, without a firstness claim.</p><p>AI tools were used extensively in solving, source comparison, adversarial verification and writing. This work is unrefereed, without external human peer review, journal acceptance or formal proof-assistant certification. The supporting kit contains the complete manuscript source, newly written exact standard-library controls, custody records and bounded source-read ledgers. Finite checks corroborate the proof and do not reconstruct historical omitted programs.</p>\n\n## Accepted scope and review\n\nFor every n\u22651, exactly all-real-spectrum Segre/Jordan types occur on a nonempty open set of R^n for smooth compactly supported real Nijenhuis tensors; arbitrary numerical real eigenvalues and block partitions allowed in commuting local frame.\n\nNo original smooth algebraic-type gap asserted. Necessity and previously known semisimple/2D cases credited; arbitrary real Jordan construction is candidate contribution. Source locator 5.9 reconciled to primary v2 Problem5.11/v1 Problem4.10; no Cartesian-frame or globally constant type claim.\n\nThe result is accepted at the exact audited head `954dd70b49458026e29b8dae63243391249008d8`. 2 fresh independent complete AI whole-package reviews were completed, with the final review finding zero actionable issues. Subsequent bounded administrative adoption is recorded in the current external ROOT final seal; earlier status/counter/hold fields remain dated history. Prior mathematical results and proof dependencies are credited. Historical novelty and worldwide current openness are unestablished. AI tools were used extensively; this is an unrefereed preprint, without conventional human peer review or formal proof certification.\n\nThe repository Zenodo uploader verified the exact reviewed metadata and PDF/support bytes. The Google Workspace CLI recorded the DOI/details in the requested tracker with exact read-back. No GitHub release is created. Current audit and publication receipts: `audits/pr1094_2100509`.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Preserved original PR description: dated submission history</summary>\n\n## Complete smooth classification with credited prior obstruction\n\nFor every n >= 1, exactly the all-real-spectrum Segre/Jordan types occur on a\nnonempty open subset of R^n for a smooth compactly supported real Nijenhuis\n(1,1)-tensor. The construction permits arbitrary prescribed numerical real\neigenvalues, multiplicities, equality patterns and Jordan block sizes. Type\nchanges away from the realization domain are allowed.\n\nThe full analytic proof includes the torus-collar torsion identity, finite\nordered arrow deletion and scalar drift for every Jordan block, smooth\nendpoint plateaus, same-dimensional torus embedding and exact zero extension.\nThe independent written audit and acceptance accompany the proof. Aggregate\nfinite checks are supporting metadata; no computational extrapolation or\nomitted executable is a premise of the general theorem.\n\nNecessity is credited to Bolsinov\u2013Konyaev\u2013Matveev, Nijenhuis Geometry,\nTheorem 6.1: https://arxiv.org/abs/1903.04603v2 . The real semisimple and\ntwo-dimensional Jordan cases were already credited by the original problem\nsource. The exact primary locator is Problem 5.11, PDF page 29, in\nhttps://arxiv.org/abs/1804.03737v2 ; the earlier v1 is Problem 4.10, PDF page 37.\nThe corpus label 5.9 is not substituted for either primary locator.\n\n## Distribution and review limits\n\nExactly eight authored proof/audit/acceptance/status and public-source-review\nor metadata files are added under `unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/2100509/`.\nAll mathematical statements, arguments, examples and qualifications are\npreserved. Editorial changes remove private workflow/revision provenance,\nreplace unavailable script references with permitted aggregate metadata,\nstate review limits and bind the public proof and audit exactly.\n\nThis AI-assisted, unrefereed edition claims no bibliographic priority,\nexhaustive preexisting-current-openness certificate, external human peer\nreview, journal acceptance or formal proof-assistant certification. Programs,\nraw generated outputs, datasets, copied third-party source bodies or images,\nand private coordination material are excluded. Recorded scholarly inspection\nhistory is not a new retrieval, source rehash, inspection or literature search\nby edition preparation.\n\nQUEUE.md and unrelated entries remain unchanged. Editorial preparation adds\nno substantive proof turn and resets no historical accounting. No merge,\nrelease, DOI or outside outreach is requested.\n\nBase commit: `f6caddda8f8be2cdb3e91494325d8f7f365bc3fc`.\n\n## Exact distributed file identities\n\n- `ACCEPTANCE.json`: 1,661 bytes; SHA-256 `3fd00339eafc3793e9a433a72d6aca969b284bc1ce4bb902e288ee316e238ce0`.\n- `MANIFEST.json`: 1,608 bytes; SHA-256 `027426bd03416c58be8c3bd768fa57a776c68bc0cb96963ff3beb1bdf5d7fd8d`.\n- `MATHEMATICAL_AUDIT.md`: 15,880 bytes; SHA-256 `ac3f95ee68cf928c7e5862e522aae015d76db3ad84bdf6a06436ffa6be165b8c`.\n- `MATHEMATICAL_REPORT.md`: 10,006 bytes; SHA-256 `b8dda0f0c82f5f0f8bd0c8de608b2a6ddee4e11b4267311ba0ef1d8aedf4486f`.\n- `README.md`: 3,855 bytes; SHA-256 `63431e38fa8c6d0e70e813f440fda14f713d8e08d04fd89ab3ce171fc5b84a9f`.\n- `SOURCE_METADATA.json`: 6,985 bytes; SHA-256 `cd798875c3e1b52850c358115f00b65d4ae0643257ada45739b0985853ff1ab5`.\n- `SOURCE_REVIEW.md`: 4,603 bytes; SHA-256 `be9f4dabf8f0f4ddaa8fbeab429ebcbe439565037183a3c9c5a11f458ee00b1a`.\n- `STATUS.json`: 1,296 bytes; SHA-256 `32ebda8f9707d0d32f1145d80827b0423204dd85cb320aae2a0e57a3e5b4a880`.\n\nThe manifest lists eight members and hashes the other seven; this body pins the manifest independently.\n\n\n</details>\n",
